diff --git a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
index e9ea7168..1867aaca 100644
--- a/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
+++ b/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md
@@ -1097,6 +1097,21 @@ read again first: when the primary display changes, so do all coordinates, and
 apps post nothing. macOS says nothing either when the Dock or the menu bar changes
 size or hides, so each layout starts by reading the display's visible frame.
 
+A floating window's frame is its person's, with one exception (`collab/QUESTIONS.md`, Q20): a change of displays
+after which less than half of it shows. A window that no display shows at all counts as out of view, which is
+what fetches it. One of which a quarter shows does not, and must not, because people push windows aside until a
+strip is left; so no way back had anything to fetch. Who did it can only be told while the displays change.
+`updateDisplays`, and a resume after a pause, therefore note the floating windows in view that are left like that
+(`Controller+LeftBehind.swift`), and the layout that follows fits each: one move, the least that brings it wholly
+into view, smaller only if it is larger than the display. (Where the Desktop is in view and large enough to use it
+goes onto the Desktop, squeezed if need be, like every floating window Arbor places there.) Its own frame stays
+remembered. What stays is a window the change did not touch: as much of it shows as before. On a display of
+another size that is not believed of a window that has spoken within the last half minute, whose "before" may
+have been measured too late. So the Dock, the menu bar, a lid that moves every corner and a display that grows move
+nothing. A window that cannot be moved at that moment, because its app hangs or it is in the Dock or on its flight out
+of it, is owed the move until it can be, on books of its own: `unplaced` and `owedMoves` do not say what is owed. A
+hand that moves it meanwhile has the last word, and a move of the view that takes it out of view ends the debt.
+
 ## What counts as a window
 
 Role `AXWindow`, subrole `AXStandardWindow` (`WindowKind` in ArborCore): no sheets,
